# OpenSocrates Antigravity modular content

OpenSocrates {{PRODUCT_VERSION}} uses `.agents/rules/opensocrates.md` and
`.agents/skills/opensocrates/` in the chosen workspace. The rule is `always_on`;
the full controller and {{METHOD_COUNT}} EN/KO procedures are read progressively.
Use ordinary tasks without an OpenSocrates command. Complete reads and useful
results still require a real conversation-app probe, separately from the IDE.

For a global route, map the owned rule to
`~/.gemini/config/rules/opensocrates.md` and the owned skill folder to
`~/.gemini/config/skills/opensocrates/`; the rule's relative reference remains
`../skills/opensocrates/SKILL.md`. These global locations affect both app and IDE.
Never overwrite user `GEMINI.md`, `AGENTS.md` or unrelated rules. Choose one route;
do not duplicate workspace and global entry. Restart the conversation after
disablement; deleting files does not erase context already loaded.

This artifact is modular content, not a CLI-registered plugin. It has no hooks,
runtime, launcher, credential access or telemetry. An inaccessible reference
means unavailable grounding, not permission to invent a method. Windows and
global permission behavior need separate qualification.

Content revision: {{CONTENT_REVISION}}. Canonical source identity: {{SOURCE_TREE_HASH}}.
The root `release-manifest.json` inventories the owned rule and skill files.
